# Copy to web/.env (gitignored). Which database the site reads:
#
# LOCAL SANDBOX (default for development). `python scripts/simulate_week.py`
# starts a throwaway Postgres under ~/.cache/beatvegas/pg_sim and replays a
# real week into it; it prints the URL to paste here. Renders against it cost
# nothing and cannot touch the live picks ledger.
# (scripts/pg_sim.py listens on 54329 by default -- BV_SIM_PG_PORT -- not Postgres's
# usual 5432/5433, so it can never be mistaken for a real install.)
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://localhost:54329/beatvegas_sim"

# PRODUCTION (Neon). Only when you mean to read prod from a laptop: every board
# render is ~0.5 MB of metered egress, and a dev server pointed here through a
# day of refreshes is what exhausted the Free plan's 5 GB/month on 2026-09-16.
# On a network that filters Neon:5432 (campus) also set NEON_HTTP=1 — the app then
# uses Prisma's Neon serverless adapter over 443 instead of node-postgres.
# (prisma.config.ts reads this file for the CLI; the app reads the environment.)
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://<user>:<password>@<pooler-host>.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"
# NEON_HTTP=1

# The password gate and the cron dispatcher are production-only; leave unset
# locally (middleware only enforces the gate when VERCEL is set).
# APP_PASSWORD=
# CRON_SECRET=
# GITHUB_DISPATCH_TOKEN=
